# opengerminal_v1.1.0.def  —  RELEASE build (no IgLM, no GPL, no AF3)
# ===========================================================================
# Apptainer definition for OpenGerminal v1.1.0.
# Derived from germinal_free.def (v1.0.0) with the changes listed below.
# Each change is annotated with the reviewer item it addresses.
#
# CHANGES FROM v1.0.0  (see CHANGELOG for full text)
#
#   [R2-1]  The IgLM PACKAGE is absent from the release build, and the code
#           path that would use it is unreachable. Three changes were needed:
#             - `iglm` dropped from the pip install line;
#             - `from iglm import IgLM` in germinal/filters/filter_utils.py was
#               at module scope, so v1.0.0 could not import its own scoring
#               module without the package. It now lives in get_iglm_ll();
#             - `iglm` dropped from colabdesign/setup.py install_requires,
#               which would otherwise reinstall it during the editable install
#               however carefully this file avoids naming it. That line is the
#               literal source of Reviewer 2's first point.
#           colabdesign/colabdesign/iglm/ is deliberately KEPT in the source
#           tree: opengerminal_v1.1.0_bench.def bootstraps from this image and
#           adds the package back for the IgLM reference arm, so the code has
#           to be present even though it is inert without it. "Removed"
#           therefore means absent and unreachable, not stripped from source —
#           and that is what the build assertions below check.
#
#   [R3-1]  germinal/filters/af3.py DELETED from the source tree, and the
#           `af3` import removed from filters/filter_utils.py.
#           Rationale: af3.py carries a CC-BY-NC-SA 4.0 header plus the
#           AlphaFold 3 Model Parameters Terms of Use, i.e. non-commercial
#           terms travelled with the file inside a container we describe as
#           permitting unrestricted commercial use. `colabfold` is dropped
#           with it (it was imported only by af3.py) — this also removes the
#           undisclosed call to the public ColabFold MMseqs2 server.
#           NOTE: pdbfixer is installed independently via micromamba below,
#           so dropping colabfold does not break the open-source scoring path.
#
#   [R1-9]  cvxopt (GPL-3.0-or-later) removed.
#           It was inherited verbatim from the upstream Dockerfile and used
#           only by mgda() in colabdesign/af/design.py. The manuscript states
#           the method is PCGrad (Section 2.1); mgda() is unreachable under
#           every shipped and default configuration. The import is made lazy
#           in the source tree so the function still works if a user installs
#           cvxopt themselves.
#           MDAnalysis (GPL) also removed — zero imports; it pulled in
#           GridDataFormats (LGPLv3), which disappears with it.
#
#   [R1-9]  params/DAlphaBall.gcc DELETED from the source tree.
#           Rosetta-lineage binary (from BindCraft) with no licence file,
#           used only on the PyRosetta code path, which is guarded by
#           `if pr is not None` and never taken because PyRosetta is absent.
#
#   [AE-5]  params_from_sif.tar no longer copied in. AlphaFold-Multimer
#   [R1-m3] parameters are supplied at runtime by bind mount (see %help).
#           This makes "we do not redistribute the AF2 parameters" a
#           structural property of the image rather than an accident, and
#           removes the CC BY 4.0 redistribution obligation.
#
#   [AE-5]  Shipped run configs now default to structure_model: "chai",
#   [R1-11] matching the configuration actually used for every benchmark in
#           the paper. Configs are the six as-run final_config.yaml files.
#
#   [R1-M10] The v1.0.0 image contained two source edits that appear in no
#           commit at all (a multi-chain interface string and a leftover
#           "DEBUG chain_map keys" print, both in filters/pyrosetta_utils.py;
#           `git log -S` finds neither anywhere in the history). They are not
#           carried forward: that module requires PyRosetta, which this image
#           does not install, so neither edit was ever reachable and no
#           published number depends on either. Because this image is built
#           from a tagged commit rather than from a hand-edited sandbox, the
#           source tree and the image now agree file by file -- which is the
#           actual remedy for R1 major 10 and 11.
#           (The two multi-chain fixes that WERE needed, in utils/utils.py and
#           pr_alternative_utils.py, had already been committed upstream of
#           this work in 70456fc and 860a520.)
#
# Build on HPC login node:
#   module load apptainer
#   apptainer build --fakeroot opengerminal_v1.1.0.sif opengerminal_v1.1.0.def
#
# Required in the same directory as this .def file:
#   germinal_src/      the v1.1.0 source tree (git tag v1.1.0)
# ===========================================================================

Bootstrap: docker
From: nvidia/cuda:12.4.1-cudnn-runtime-ubuntu22.04

%labels
    maintainer teaninja
    version 1.1.0
    description "OpenGerminal - PyRosetta-free Germinal pipeline (release build)"
    base_image nvidia/cuda:12.4.1-cudnn-runtime-ubuntu22.04
    contains_iglm false
    contains_pyrosetta false
    contains_af3_module false
    contains_gpl_components false
    contains_af2_parameters false

%environment
    export MAMBA_ROOT_PREFIX=/opt/conda
    export MAMBA_NO_BANNER=1
    export CONDA_ENV=germinal
    export PATH=/opt/conda/envs/germinal/bin:${PATH}
    export PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1
    export MPLBACKEND=Agg
    export HYDRA_FULL_ERROR=1
    export PIP_NO_CACHE_DIR=1

%post
    # -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    # System packages
    # -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive
    apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
        ca-certificates curl git bzip2 aria2 ffmpeg procps tini \
        build-essential libssl-dev \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

    # -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Micromamba
    # -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    export MAMBA_ROOT_PREFIX=/opt/conda
    export MAMBA_NO_BANNER=1
    curl -Ls https://micro.mamba.pm/api/micromamba/linux-64/latest | \
        tar -xvj -C /usr/local/bin --strip-components=1 bin/micromamba

    micromamba create -y -n germinal python=3.10
    micromamba clean -a -y

    export PATH=/opt/conda/envs/germinal/bin:${PATH}
    export PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1
    export MPLBACKEND=Agg
    export HYDRA_FULL_ERROR=1
    export PIP_NO_CACHE_DIR=1

    # -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    # OpenMM + PDBFixer via conda-forge (best CUDA compatibility).
    # pdbfixer is installed HERE, independently of colabfold — this is why
    # dropping colabfold below does not break pr_alternative_utils.py.
    # -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    micromamba install -y -n germinal -c conda-forge \
        openmm \
        pdbfixer \
    && micromamba clean -a -y

    # -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Core Python packages
    #
    # REMOVED vs v1.0.0:  cvxopt      GPL-3.0-or-later, only used by mgda()
    #                     colabfold   only imported by the deleted af3.py
    #                     MDAnalysis  zero imports (takes GridDataFormats with it)
    # RETAINED:           mdtraj      LGPL-2.1+, imported by filters/pDockQ.py
    #                     ipsae       MIT, supplies pDockQ2 / LIS / ipSAE metrics
    #                     freesasa    MIT
    # -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    python -m pip install --upgrade pip wheel setuptools
    python -m pip install uv

    uv pip install --system \
        pandas matplotlib numpy biopython scipy seaborn tqdm ffmpeg py3dmol \
        chex dm-haiku==0.0.13 dm-tree joblib ml-collections immutabledict \
        optax mdtraj ipsae==1.0.1 freesasa

    # -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    # PyTorch (CUDA 12.4)
    # -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    uv pip install --system \
        --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu124 \
        "torch==2.6.0" \
        "torchvision==0.21.0" \
        "torchaudio==2.6.0"

    uv pip install --system torchtyping==0.1.5

    PYG_URL="https://data.pyg.org/whl/torch-2.6.0%2Bcu124.html"
    uv pip install --system "torch_geometric==2.6.*" -f "${PYG_URL}"

    # -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Antibody language model
    #
    # The pipeline imports ablang2 only. ablang2.pretrained() selects
    # 'ablang1-heavy' for VHH and 'ablang2-paired' for scFv, and ablang2
    # carries its own loader for the AbLang1 weights
    # (ablang2/load_model.py: ablang-heavy.tar.gz -> amodel.pt).
    # `ablang` is installed because ablang2 is installed --no-deps; it is not
    # on the pipeline's code path.
    #
    # Licence: ablang and ablang2 are both BSD 3-Clause (NOT Apache 2.0 as
    # stated in the v1.0.0 README, manuscript and .def file).
    # -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    uv pip install --system \
        ablang \
        ablang2==0.2.1 --no-deps

    uv pip install --system rotary_embedding_torch==0.8.9 --no-deps

    # -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Cofolding model.  NOTE: `iglm` is NOT installed in the release build.
    # See opengerminal_v1.1.0_bench.def for the benchmark-only image.
    # -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    uv pip install --system chai-lab==0.6.1

    # -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    # JAX (pinned to 0.5.3, CUDA 12 build)
    # -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    uv pip install --system jax==0.5.3
    uv pip install --system hydra-core omegaconf
    uv pip install --system \
        "jax[cuda12_pip]==0.5.3" \
        -f https://storage.googleapis.com/jax-releases/jax_cuda_releases.html

    # NOTE: PyRosetta is intentionally NOT installed. Relaxation and interface
    # scoring are provided by germinal/filters/pr_alternative_utils.py using
    # OpenMM + FASPR + FreeSASA + Biopython + sc-rs.

    # -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    # OpenGerminal source (git tag v1.1.0)
    # -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    # The staging path is /opt and NOT /tmp. Apptainer mounts the host /tmp over
    # the container's /tmp while %post runs, which hides anything %files put
    # there; the symptom is "cp: cannot stat '/tmp/.../.'" after every package
    # has already been installed. Checked explicitly rather than relying on cp
    # to fail, because a silent staging failure is how a build recipe ends up
    # describing an image it did not produce.
    test -d /opt/germinal_src || { echo "FAIL: %files did not deliver /opt/germinal_src"; exit 1; }
    test -f /opt/germinal_src/run_germinal.py || { echo "FAIL: /opt/germinal_src is not the source tree"; exit 1; }

    mkdir -p /workspace
    cp -r /opt/germinal_src/. /workspace/
    cd /workspace
    uv pip install --system -e /workspace/colabdesign
    uv pip install --system -e .

    # -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Build-time assertions.  The build FAILS if any of these do not hold.
    # These are the machine-checkable form of the claims made in the
    # manuscript and in the response to Reviewer 2 point 1.
    # -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    echo "=== verifying release invariants ==="

    ! python -c "import iglm"     2>/dev/null || { echo "FAIL: iglm importable";     exit 1; }
    ! python -c "import pyrosetta" 2>/dev/null || { echo "FAIL: pyrosetta importable"; exit 1; }
    ! python -c "import cvxopt"   2>/dev/null || { echo "FAIL: cvxopt importable";   exit 1; }
    ! python -c "import MDAnalysis" 2>/dev/null || { echo "FAIL: MDAnalysis importable"; exit 1; }
    ! python -c "import colabfold" 2>/dev/null || { echo "FAIL: colabfold importable"; exit 1; }

    test ! -e /workspace/germinal/filters/af3.py       || { echo "FAIL: af3.py present";        exit 1; }
    test ! -e /workspace/params/DAlphaBall.gcc         || { echo "FAIL: DAlphaBall present";    exit 1; }

    # The IgLM source stays in the tree on purpose (the benchmark image adds the
    # package back for the reference arm), so grepping for the string would fail
    # here by design and prove nothing. The invariant is REACHABILITY, and it has
    # two halves, both of which v1.0.0 would have failed:
    #   - the scoring module must import with no iglm installed. In v1.0.0 it
    #     could not: filter_utils.py imported IgLM at module scope.
    #   - the ColabDesign hook must be None, so ablm_model: iglm cannot run.
    # The benchmark image asserts the mirror image of the second line.
    python -c "import germinal.filters.filter_utils" \
        || { echo "FAIL: filter_utils does not import without iglm"; exit 1; }
    python -c "from colabdesign.af.prep import CustomIgLM; assert CustomIgLM is None" \
        || { echo "FAIL: CustomIgLM is not None in the release image"; exit 1; }

    python -c "import ablang2, chai_lab, openmm, freesasa, pdbfixer, mdtraj; print('imports OK')"
    python -c "import ablang2; print('ablang2', ablang2.__version__ if hasattr(ablang2,'__version__') else 'n/a')"

    echo "=== release invariants OK ==="

    mkdir -p /workspace/params /workspace/pdbs /workspace/results

    # -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Cleanup
    # -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    micromamba clean -a -y
    pip cache purge 2>/dev/null || true
    rm -rf /opt/germinal_src

%files
    # v1.1.0 source tree only. params_from_sif.tar is deliberately NOT
    # included — AF-Multimer parameters are supplied at runtime (see %help).
    #
    # Staged under /opt, not /tmp: the host /tmp is mounted over the container's
    # /tmp during %post, so a file staged at /tmp/... is not there when %post
    # tries to read it. The source path is relative to the directory the build
    # is invoked from, so build from the directory that contains germinal_src/.
    germinal_src /opt/germinal_src

%runscript
    exec python /workspace/run_germinal.py "$@"

%help
    OpenGerminal v1.1.0 — PyRosetta-free Germinal antibody design pipeline.

    WHAT THIS IMAGE DOES NOT CONTAIN
        PyRosetta            replaced by OpenMM + FASPR + FreeSASA + Biopython + sc-rs
        IgLM                 removed; the language model is AbLang
        AlphaFold 3 module   removed (non-commercial terms)
        cvxopt (GPL-3.0)     removed; gradient merging uses PCGrad
        AlphaFold2 params    NOT bundled — supply at runtime, see below

    ANTIBODY LANGUAGE MODEL
        package        ablang2 v0.2.1
        model (VHH)    ablang1-heavy
        model (scFv)   ablang2-paired
        weights        ablang-heavy.tar.gz -> amodel.pt
                       sha256 ab0888f7dc5e89fbf10568a100f081eadf9386bd460d3cdf1d6731044a01266b
        licence        BSD 3-Clause

    REQUIRED RUNTIME BIND MOUNTS
        AlphaFold-Multimer parameters are required by Stage 1 (gradient
        hallucination) and are ~5.4 GB, so they are not baked into the image:

          --bind /path/to/af_params:/workspace/params

        Obtain them once with:
          aria2c -x 16 https://storage.googleapis.com/alphafold/alphafold_params_2022-12-06.tar
        The parameters are CC BY 4.0 (DeepMind relicensed them in January 2022).

        Other mounts:
          --bind /path/to/pdbs:/workspace/pdbs
          --bind /path/to/results:/workspace/results
          --bind /path/to/chai_cache:/opt/conda/envs/germinal/lib/python3.10/site-packages/downloads
          --bind /path/to/ablang_weights:/opt/conda/envs/germinal/lib/python3.10/site-packages/ablang2/model-weights-ablang1-heavy

    EXAMPLE
        apptainer exec --nv \
          --bind $PARAMS:/workspace/params \
          --bind $PDBS:/workspace/pdbs \
          --bind $RESULTS:/workspace/results \
          opengerminal_v1.1.0.sif \
          python run_germinal.py run=vhh_pdl1 target=pdl1 experiment_name=exp1

    KNOWN APPROXIMATIONS
        Three PyRosetta-derived interface metrics retain placeholder values
        because the energy units cannot be mapped to OpenMM output without
        recalibration:
            binder_score     -1.0    recorded only; also used by Stage 2 selection
            interface_dG    -10.0    recorded only, not a filter threshold
            interface_hbonds    5    SEE BELOW
        Two further placeholders are inherited from upstream Germinal's
        Chai-1 integration:
            chain_ptm          1.0
            chain_iptm         1.0

        interface_hbonds is fixed at 5, which is above the Stage 4 threshold
        of >= 3, so that filter always passes. Filter thresholds inherited
        from Germinal were calibrated against PyRosetta energies and SHOULD BE
        RECALIBRATED against your own benchmark data before use.
